INT. ULYSSES HOUSE - UPPER CHAMBER - NIGHT

PENELOPE, dark-haired, stately, worn with waiting, sleeps sweetly at the gates of dreamland. The phantom IPHTHIME hovers over her head in the likeness of her sister, come through the hole where the thong pulls the door to.

(SOUND: night insects, the thong-hole whispering)

PENELOPE
Sister, why have you come here? You do not come very often, but I suppose that is because you live such a long way off.

Her sleeping face draws tight.

PENELOPE (CONT'D)
Am I, then, to leave off crying and refrain from all the sad thoughts that torture me?

PENELOPE (CONT'D)
I, who have lost my brave and lion-hearted husband, who had every good quality under heaven, and whose name was great over all Hellas and middle Argos.

A breath like a sob, still inside the dream.

PENELOPE (CONT'D)
And now my darling son has gone off on board of a ship—a foolish fellow who has never been used to roughing it, nor to going about among gatherings of men.

PENELOPE (CONT'D)
I am even more anxious about him than about my husband.

PENELOPE (CONT'D)
I am all in a tremble lest he come to something among the people he is going to visit, or at sea, for he has many enemies who are plotting against him.

The dim phantom does not sit. It hangs in the dark above the bed.

IPHTHIME
Take heart, and be not so much dismayed. There is one gone with him whom many another would have wished to have for a friend.

IPHTHIME (CONT'D)
Even Pallas Minerva, who has compassion upon you and has come to his rescue. I will not tell you yet whether he is alive or dead, and there is no use in idle conversation.

PENELOPE
Sister, I am much obliged, but tell me about that other unhappy one. Is he still alive, or is he already dead and in the house of Hades?

IPHTHIME
I shall tell you truly. I know nothing about him, whether he is alive or dead, and it is bad to talk idly about such things.

On this the phantom vanishes through the thong-hole of the door and goes back toward the house of Hades.

(SOUND: air sucked through the thong-hole, then PENELOPE starting awake)

PENELOPE starts up from her sleep. For a moment she stares at the empty dark above the bed. Her heart is comforted, so vivid has been her dream.

EXT. ITHACA HARBOUR - NIGHT

The same black ship that waited off the coast. ANTINOUS, handsome, insolent, the cruel mouth set, goes on board with the other SUITORS. Twenty men take the benches. They push out, intent on murdering TELEMACHUS.

(SOUND: oars finding tholes, a hull sliding off pebbles)

No one calls a name. The strait takes them.

EXT. ASTERIS ISLET - NIGHT

A rocky islet of no great size, mid channel between Ithaca and Samos. A harbour on either side where a ship can lie. The SUITORS bring their vessel in under the lee and kill the sail. Arms are stacked in the shadow of the rock. They place themselves in ambush.

(SOUND: canvas coming down, water slapping two small harbours, bronze set quietly on stone)

The channel runs on either hand, empty yet. They wait for a boy to come home.

